## <programme>/notes/rc2-2026-11-01/sr/REPORT.md, lines 133 to 175
### What grew, and which engine files it holds

Relative to main, two budgeted items grew: the engine chunk's static
closure and `/birth-chart/` (both builds). Every other route is the same or
smaller; the largest chunks are byte for byte main's.

The engine chunk's closure, all eight chunks (33,361 bytes):

| Site chunk | Gzip | Holds | Against rc.1 |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `full.AUZx8EGL.js` | 313 | the site's `src/lib/engine/full.ts` | site code; new name because its imports changed |
| `chart-adapter.D7gaZnvr.js` | 304 | the site's `src/lib/engine/chart-adapter.ts` | site code |
| `rolldown-runtime.DK3Fl9T5.js` | 154 | the bundler's runtime | |
| `chunk-B5LKF437.7_bxrzb_.js` | 6,537 | `dist/chunk-BHJXUY67.js` (`deltat.ts`) and `dist/chunk-B5LKF437.js` (`reference-span.ts`, `time-scale-data.ts`, `time-scale.ts`) | both files byte-identical to rc.1's |
| `chunk-NIRYKLHT.Bm5YfgXm.js` | 22,989 | `dist/chunk-2BB5GQ3P.js` (`nutation.ts`, `frame.ts`), astronomy-engine 2.1.19 `esm/astronomy.js`, `dist/chunk-NIRYKLHT.js` (`body-label.ts`, `exact.ts`, `declination.ts`, `points.ts`, `ephemeris.ts`) | new files; in rc.1 all seven modules were the ephemeris chunk `dist/chunk-W2TMLFJ3.js`; still one site chunk |
| `chunk-NNOSOOWS.CflCEcE2.js` | 1,781 | `dist/chunk-NNOSOOWS.js` (`houses.ts`) | rc.1's `dist/chunk-VDVUUMY2.js`, same 11,639 bytes; now imports signs from the next row |
| `chunk-F4JKI3XV.DXFJXQuL.js` | 745 | `dist/chunk-F4JKI3XV.js` (`aspects.ts`, `types.ts`) | **new chunk**: rc.1 held `aspects.ts`, `signs.ts` and `types.ts` in one file, `dist/chunk-YJ7WZ7NS.js` |
| `chunk-RMBWKZI2.DZR4n1wo.js` | 538 | `dist/chunk-RMBWKZI2.js` (`signs.ts`) | **new chunk**, the other half of that split |

`/birth-chart/` holds three engine-bearing chunks, `chunk-F4JKI3XV`,
`chunk-NNOSOOWS` and `chunk-RMBWKZI2` (3,064 bytes); in rc.1 it would have
held two, the chunks of `chunk-YJ7WZ7NS.js` and `chunk-VDVUUMY2.js`. Its other
41 chunks (42 with the daily-email island) hold no engine module.

**The code did not grow.** Split by tsup's `// src/<file>` markers, every
source module in these chunks has the same code in rc.1 and rc.2 apart from
renamed locals (`RAD4` to `RAD3` and the like, which minification renames
anyway) and `ENGINE_VERSION` ("1.1.0-rc.1" to "1.1.0-rc.2", same length)
(`tools/module-sections.mjs`). The growth is structural: to let `./time` load
the signs, the nutation and the frame without the ephemeris, rc.2 splits
`signs.ts` out of the chunk it shared with `aspects.ts` and `types.ts`, and
moves `nutation.ts` and `frame.ts` out of the ephemeris chunk (as the rc.2
evidence README, *Sizes*, says). In the site the first split adds one static
chunk to the engine closure and to `/birth-chart/` (one more gzip stream and
the import and export statements that join the parts); the second stays
inside one site chunk.

**The same split shrinks seven routes** (`/`, `/transits/`,
`/solar-return/`, `/lunar-return/`, `/today/`, `/compatibility/`,
`/registry/collection/`) by 0.3 to 0.5 KB: their only engine-bearing chunk is
now `chunk-F4JKI3XV` (aspects and types, 745 bytes), where rc.1 gave them the
chunk of `chunk-YJ7WZ7NS.js`, which also carried the signs code the engine
needs elsewhere.
